%N A057210 Number of fullerenes with 2n vertices (or carbon atoms), counting enantiomorphic pairs as distinct.
%C A057210 The b-file supplied in 2006 was computed with a version of fullgen predating the bug fix described in A007894; its values a(68)-a(100) were too small. See the b-file link for corrected and extended values. - _Tyler Satchel Orden_, Aug 07 2026
%D A057210 P. W. Fowler and D. E. Manolopoulos, An Atlas of Fullerenes, Cambridge Univ. Press, 1995, see p. 32.
%H A057210 Tyler Satchel Orden, <a href="/A057210/b057210.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 10..200</a> (terms from Engel, Smillie & Goedgebeur, 2025; terms a(10)-a(67) from Gunnar Brinkmann, 2006)
%H A057210 Philip Engel and Peter Smillie <a href="https://doi.org/10.2140/gt.2018.22.2839">The number of convex tilings of the sphere by triangles, squares, or hexagons</a>, Geom. Topol., 22 (2018), 2839-2864; arXiv:<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.02614">1702.02614</a> [math.GT], 2017-2018.
%H A057210 Philip Engel, Jan Goedgebeur, and Peter Smillie, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1215/00127094-2024-0037">Exact enumeration of fullerenes</a>, Duke Math. J., 174 (2025), 575-613; arXiv:<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.01655">2304.01655</a> [math.GT], 2023-2024.
%F A057210 a(n) = (809/1306069401600)*sigma_9(n) + O(n^8) where sigma_9(n) is the ninth divisor power sum, A013957. - _Philip Engel_, Nov 29 2017
